{
 "about": "Lot 313 (external bug hunt, edition 1.4: BUG-85; the mini-hunt's variants): busybox runs the program its argv names, read as busybox reads it \u2014 `busybox sh -i`, `/bin/busybox sh`, the login shells `-sh` and `-ash`, a link named for its shell (`ln -s /bin/busybox ~/sh`), a name starting with `busybox` (`busybox.static sh`), busybox through busybox, a path after busybox \u2014 each with its stdin and stdout on a socket a web server's process connected out: R020 (Critical, its kill held); busybox sh on a pty whose parent holds that socket: R020's third shape. Controls: busybox's nc and cat, its --help, a link whose name is no program: nothing. On main only `sh`/`ash` in argv[0] was read: `busybox sh`, `-sh`, `-ash` had no shape. The renamed copy of an installed shell (N1) needs the exec pump's content check, which a replay has not: its unit tests and the lab cover it.",
 "fires": [
  "R020_ShellWithSocketStdio"
 ],
 "held": [
  "R020_ShellWithSocketStdio"
 ],
